    """Summarize a collection of integers as comma-separated ranges.

    `nums` may be unsorted and contain duplicates; it is treated as a set and
    must not be modified. Sort the distinct values and group them into runs
    of consecutive integers:
      - a run of three or more integers is written "start-end";
      - a run of exactly two integers is written as two separate items "a,b";
      - a single integer is written on its own.
